{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "PHP Data Types"}, {"type": "position", "content": 9}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear and use in PHP data types."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understand information about common solutions to problems in spoken or written documents.   Talk about programming and data base related to hypertext preprocessor in spoken or written documents. "}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.  Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe7n8le01ob09re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Past, Present, and Future Continuous Review"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We use statements in different tenses to talk about experiences in our lives."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">The present continuous tense</span>: Remember that we use the present continuous tense to talk about actions that are currently happening. <br/><br/> Grammatical structure: <br/><br/>  <div class=\"center_text\"> Subject + <span class=\"strong\">auxiliary verb to be</span> + <span class=\"strong\">main verb (-ing form)</span> + complement </div> <br/><br/> Examples: <br/><span class=\"italic\"> I <span class=\"strong\">am trying</span> to understand the difference between PHP data types. <br/> She<span class=\"strong\"> is studying</span> the different PHP data types. </span><br/><br/><br/> <span class=\"strong\">The past continuous tense</span>: We use the past continuous tense to talk about actions that started in the past and were in progress until something stopped them. <br/><br/> Grammatical structure: <br/><br/> <div class=\"center_text\"> Subject + <span class=\"strong\">auxiliary verb to be in past</span> + <span class=\"strong\">main verb (-ing form)</span> + complement</div> <br/><br/> Example: <br/><span class=\"italic\"> People <span class=\"strong\">were having</span> problems creating dynamic content before the creation of PHP.</span><br/><br/><br/> <span class=\"strong\">The future continuous tense</span>: We use the future continuous tense to talk about actions that will start and have a continuity in the future. <br/><br/> Grammatical structure: <br/><br/> <div class=\"center_text\"> Subject + <span class=\"strong\">will</span> + <span class=\"strong\">be</span> + <span class=\"strong\">main verb (-ing form)</span> + complement</div><br/><br/> Example: <br/><span class=\"italic\"> Web designers <span class=\"strong\"> will be applying</span> upgrades on PHP in the years to come. </span><br/>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'm just studying for a test. How are you?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I was thinking that PHP is easier than Java and also many big companies prefer to use it. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You'll be working in one of them someday."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Third Conditional in Affirmative"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">the third conditional</span> or \u201cunreal past\u201d to talk about situations that never happened and the possible results of said situations."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The <span class=\"strong\"> third conditional</span> is useful when we want to speculate about situations that could have been possible if something else had occurred. There are two ways to build this kind of statements: <br/><br/> <ol><li><span class=\"strong\"> Beginning with an if clause:</li> </span><br/><br/><div class=\"center_text\"> If + subject + <span class=\"strong\"> had</span> + <span class=\"strong\">main verb in past participle</span> + complement + comma (,) + subject + <span class=\"strong\">would have</span> + <span class=\"strong\"> main verb in past participle</span> + complement</div> <br/><br/> Example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">If I <span class=\"strong\">had learned</span> about PHP in high school, I <span class=\"strong\"> would have chosen</span> to be a systems engineer. </span><br/><br/><br/> <span class=\"strong\"> <li> Beginning with the result clause (no need to add a comma):</li></span> <br/><br/> <div class=\"center_text\">Subject + <span class=\"strong\"> would have</span> + <span class=\"strong\">main verb in past participle</span> + complement + if + subject + <span class=\"strong\">had</span> + <span class=\"strong\">main verb in past participle</span> + complement</div> <br/><br/> Example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\"> would have chosen</span> to be a systems engineer If I <span class=\"strong\"> had learned</span> about PHP in high school. </span><br/>  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "If I had studied about PHP earlier, I would have obtained better jobs."}, {"type": "example", "content": "There are some things you have to know to master PHP, though. If I had known this before, I would have studied them in depth."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If your teacher had asked you to talk about arrays, you would have mentioned that they work with multiple values."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "PHP "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "(Hypertext Preprocessor) it refers to a scripting language that allows you to create web pages in an interactive way. It was developed by Rasmus Lerdorf in 1994"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  For example, PH